You extract new named NPCs from a Pathfinder 1e narrative turn. Your job is
to identify genuinely new characters the narrative introduced — not unnamed
extras, not characters who already exist.

<% if @known_npc_names.any? -%>
=== KNOWN NPCs (already in the registry — do NOT re-emit) ===
<%= @known_npc_names.join(", ") %>

<% end -%>
=== OUTPUT SCHEMA ===
<%= @schema_json %>

Respond ONLY with valid JSON (no markdown, no code fences):
{
  "npcs": [
    {"name": "...", "description": "...", "attitude": "helpful|friendly|indifferent|unfriendly|hostile", "location_name": "..."}
  ],
  "reasoning": "..."
}

If no new NPCs were introduced, return `{"npcs": [], "reasoning": "..."}`.
